# runs-ui

## sorting
- label: sortSessionList orders every sort key (recent, duration, cost, tokens, errors, files, commits, chapters, grade) highest first, and the same key with an -asc suffix (e.g. cost-asc) lowest first; rows with no value (0) sort last in both directions
  id: rsdir
  command: node --input-type=module -e "import { sortSessionList } from './src/filter/filter-formats.js'; const z = sortSessionList([{ durationMs: 0 }, { durationMs: 5 }, { durationMs: 2 }], 'duration-asc').map((r) => r.durationMs).join(''); if (z !== '250') { console.error('zero', z); process.exit(1); } const rows = [1, 3, 2].map((n) => ({ mtime: n * 1000, durationMs: n, totalTokens: n, errors: n, files: n, commits: n, chapters: n, inputTokens: n * 1e6, model: 'claude-sonnet-4' })); for (const k of ['recent', 'duration', 'cost', 'tokens', 'errors', 'files', 'commits', 'chapters']) { const d = sortSessionList(rows.slice(), k).map((r) => r.durationMs).join(''); const a = sortSessionList(rows.slice(), k + '-asc').map((r) => r.durationMs).join(''); if (d !== '321' || a !== '123') { console.error(k, d, a); process.exit(1); } } const gr = [{ id: 'bad', chapters: 1, errors: 5, toolCounts: { Bash: 6 } }, { id: 'good', chapters: 1, errors: 0 }]; if (sortSessionList(gr.slice(), 'grade')[0].id !== 'good' || sortSessionList(gr.slice(), 'grade-asc')[0].id !== 'bad') { console.error('grade'); process.exit(1); }"
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, sorting, implemented]
- label: On /sessions the table header's When, Duration, Tokens, Cost and Grade labels are buttons that sort the list by that column (highest or newest first); clicking the sorted column again flips it to lowest or oldest first, and the sorted column shows its direction with an arrow
  id: rshead
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, sorting, implemented]
- label: The Display menu's sort entries and the header buttons are one sort state, carried in ?sort= (e.g. ?sort=cost-asc) so reload, Back and the embedded first page keep both the column and the direction; choosing the active entry again flips its direction
  id: rsurl
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, sorting, implemented]

## section switching
- label: On /insights, idle g then r, g then c and g then i switch sections as on the other pages (not while typing in a field, and not when Character keys is turned off), so keyboard switching never dead-ends on Insights
  id: rsins
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, section-switch, implemented]
- label: In a hub, clicking Chat, Runs or Insights in the top bar from any of those three pages, at 756, 1280, 1512 and 1728px wide, opens that section (Chat /run, Runs /sessions, Insights /insights) with its tab marked current; Chat never lands on Insights
  id: rsnav
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test test/browser/hub-section-nav.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, section-switch, hub, implemented]

## search box
- label: The top-bar search box shrinks with the bar instead of overflowing it — at every width from 360 to 1440px the whole box lies inside the viewport, the page does not scroll sideways, and its placeholder is never cut to a single letter
  id: rssrch
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, search-box, implemented]

## launcher
- label: The New run dialog scrolls inside its overlay when it is taller than the viewport, so Start is reachable on a short screen (390x420)
  id: rslscr
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, launcher, implemented]
- label: A folder POST /api/runs rejects is reported under the Folder field in plain words naming that folder, the field is marked aria-invalid and focused, and editing the field clears the error
  id: rslerr
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, launcher, implemented]
- label: After a failed Start, focus stays inside the New run dialog (on the field at fault, otherwise Start), and the start shortcut hint names Ctrl rather than the Command key off macOS
  id: rslfoc
  tags: [spec, runs-ui, launcher, implemented]
